The '''2025 EFL Cup final''' was the final match of the [[2024–25 EFL Cup]]. It was played between [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] and [[Newcastle United F.C.|Newcastle United]] at [[Wembley Stadium]] in London, England, on 16 March 2025.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bonn |first1=Kyle |title=When is the 2025 Carabao Cup final? Date, kickoff time of League Cup title match at Wembley Stadium |url=https://www.sportingnews.com/uk/football/news/carabao-cup-final-2025-date-kickoff-time-league-cup/f25d47afa6208d8e3d433659 |website=[[The Sporting News]] |date=5 February 2025}}</ref> It was the 65th [[EFL Cup final]] and the 18th to be played at the rebuilt Wembley.<ref name="RSSSF">{{cite web |first=James M. |last=Ross |title=England - Football League Cup Finals |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tablese/engleagcuphist.html |website=Rec.Sport.Soccer Statistics Foundation |date=17 March 2025 |access-date=17 March 2025 |archive-date=17 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250317150156/https://www.rsssf.org/tablese/engleagcuphist.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

Newcastle United won the match 2–1 to secure their first EFL Cup title, their first major trophy since the [[1968–69 Inter-Cities Fairs Cup]] and their first major domestic trophy since the [[1954–55 FA Cup]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c62zl58dg8qt|title=Liverpool 1-2 Newcastle: Magpies win Carabao Cup to end 70-year domestic trophy wait|first=Phil|last=McNulty|author-link=Phil McNulty|date=16 March 2025|work=BBC Sport|accessdate=19 March 2025}}</ref>

