As a Premier League club involved in [[UEFA club competitions|UEFA competitions]], Liverpool entered in the third round and were drawn at home to fellow Premier League club [[West Ham United F.C.|West Ham United]]. The match was played at [[Anfield]] on 25 September 2024, where Liverpool won 5–1 thanks to goals from [[Diogo Jota]], [[Mohamed Salah]] and [[Cody Gakpo]] and goal for West Ham from an [[own goal]] by [[Jarell Quansah]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Johnston |first1=Neil |title=Liverpool vs West Ham United: League Cup |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c870dv9gx7zt |work=BBC Sport |date=25 September 2024 |access-date=6 February 2025 }}</ref> In the fourth round, they were drawn away to Premier League club [[Brighton & Hove Albion F.C.|Brighton & Hove Albion]], played at [[Falmer Stadium]] on 30 October 2024. The match finished with a 3–2 victory for Liverpool, with Gakpo and [[Luis Díaz (footballer, born 1997)|Luis Díaz]] both getting on the scoresheet for Liverpool and [[Simon Adingra]] and [[Tariq Lamptey]] scoring for Brighton.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Rose |first1=Gary |title=Gakpo scores twice as holders Liverpool beat Brighton to progress |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c5yrr5zdgzpt |work=BBC Sport |date=30 October 2024 |access-date=6 February 2025 }}</ref> 

In the quarter-finals, Liverpool were drawn away to Premier League club [[Southampton F.C.|Southampton]], played at [[St Mary's Stadium]] on 18 December 2024. Liverpool recorded a 2–1 victory, with goals coming from [[Darwin Núñez]] and [[Harvey Elliott]] after a Southampton goal from [[Cameron Archer]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Brotherton |first1=Alex |title=Southampton 1–2 Liverpool: Darwin Nunez scores as Reds reach Carabao Cup semi-finals |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cx2wjjk2678t |work=BBC Sport |date=18 December 2024 |access-date=6 February 2025 }}</ref> In the semi-finals, played over two legs, Liverpool were drawn against Premier League club [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]], with the first leg played away at the [[Tottenham Hotspur Stadium]] on 8 January 2025. Tottenham won the match 1–0 after a late goal by [[Lucas Bergvall]], in a match fuelled with controversy after Liverpool claimed that Bergvall should have been shown a red card for a second yellow card before the goal was scored.<ref>{{cite web |last1=McNulty |first1=Phil |title=Tottenham 1–0 Liverpool: Lucas Bergvall scores late winner as Spurs beat Liverpool in Carabao Cup semi-final |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cd608x6l01dt |work=BBC Sport |date=8 January 2025 |access-date=6 February 2025 }}</ref> The second leg was played at Anfield on 6 February, where Liverpool produced a dominant display to record a 4–0 victory, with goals coming from Gakpo, Salah, [[Dominik Szoboszlai]] and [[Virgil van Dijk]]. As a result, Liverpool won the tie 4–1 on aggregate to progress to their second consecutive EFL Cup final, and their third in four seasons.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Anderson |first1=Jess |title=Liverpool vs Tottenham LIVE |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/cn8y2xv4ygqt |work=BBC Sport |date=6 February 2025 |access-date=6 February 2025 }}</ref>

